  workarounds to get this movie made  because the film was shot during Peak  covid they weren't able to do any  rehearsals in person they were all over  Zoom the movie was shot mostly in Canada  with the exteriors shot in New York but  getting into Canada at that time proved  to be a major challenge the only reason  Milo got to collaborate with her co-star  Kiara was because she was a producer on  the film I was able to watch the dailies  every day and so I got to see all of her  performance and pick up on like little  things the two of them hardly ever got  to meet up in person because of the  restrictions covet placed on production  the easiest thing for her to do was  bring those little things she saw in her  performance into her own depiction of  the character number 7. Jessica Knowles  started writing this script in 2015  being new to filmmaking at the time she  didn't expect there to be so many drafts  there are so many people who are a part  of this project who need to be able to  sign off it she had to go from the  director to Mila Kunis to the executives  and to the producers with each draft  hoping for a green light the hardest  thing is throwing really good material  away throughout the process Jessica had  to cut so much of what people would  still consider a ton of great writing  number eight the comment that won  everyone over director Mike Barker  Jessica Knoll and Mila Kunis all met for  the first time on Zoom as sort of an  introductory call it was basically a way  for Jessica and Mike to decide if they  wanted Mila to work on the project with  them Mila recently watched a ton of  Mike's previous films and her comment on  them was what made the two of them fall  in love with her my cat a tendency to  work on really hard beautiful stories  but they were ultimately really sad and  not for everybody and not always  palatable so I was like Mike you're  really depressing they were both really  impressed by her bold statement and  wanted to continue to work with her from  then on number nine over 1500 people  auditioned to play the high school  version of Annie when Jessica Knowles  saw Kiara's audition she knew right away  that she was the one for the role I saw  there was such a vulnerability about her  that was so beautiful to me and so  necessary for this character but also  you could tell there was spunk there  which we needed this character very much  to have when Chiara landed the role she  had an introductory Zoom call with  Jessica and Mila she was absolutely  Terror terrified but found the women to  be so nice and supportive they developed  an incredible working relationship  together throughout the duration of the  film number 10. the process of bringing  the character to the screen came with  major changes and the biggest thing that  we had to do was to separate Jess from  the character when it came to writing  the novel Jessica Knoll mainly did that  entire process alone but when it came to  creating the film it was so  collaborative that Mike and Mila ended  up having major input on Annie's new  character and in turn the ending of the  film as far as I put the North Star for  the character it very much is the ending  number 11 she described herself as cheap  labor on the project I can't imagine  anyone else touching this considering  this book was based on Jessica Noel's  own trauma writing it became a way for  her to process and heal after over a  year of struggling to put the words to  paper and I think also a big part of it  was like a lot of my own story is  embedded one day I just sat down and the  voice of Annie Finelli just poured out  of me and it was non-stop for the next  eight months until the book was was  completed the studio allowed her to have  free reign over her own story as she  continued to pull from her real-life  experiences to shape it into something  that truly resonated with its audience  number 12 sometimes the darkest events  make for the most important Stories the  inspiration behind this novel is not a  happy one but what really sparked the  story was how Jessica was treated in the  aftermath of it so I was really you know  blamed and shamed  um and and really silent when she  confided in a doctor and even tried to  confront one of her attackers nobody  believed her people just were like no  it's just too complicated this story was  really important when it came to  overcoming the silence that was forced  upon her that's not what happened it was  a party it got out of hand and continues  to help thousands of people have the  courage to share their own stories and  process similar traumas they have faced  with an All-Star cast a dedicated crew  and writer the film luckiest girl alive  proves to be an incredibly success  successful collaborative personal  narrative that speaks volumes to people  who have often felt powerless when it  came to telling their own stories
 

